    <string name="is_g_goal_t">Your goal</string>
    <string name="is_g_goal">Build a holiday empire and outlast your rivals. A company goes bankrupt when its balance stays below the bank\'s limit for 3 months in a row. Its buildings are then auctioned off.</string>
    <string name="is_g_tourists_t">Tourists</string>
    <string name="is_g_tourists" formatted="false">Tourists come in three classes. Budget tourists are many but spend little and watch prices closely. Middle-class tourists are the backbone. Luxury tourists are few, spend a lot and care most about quality and location. The number of tourists grows by 0.1% every month.</string>
    <string name="is_g_season_t">Seasons</string>
    <string name="is_g_season">July and August are peak season: almost three times as many tourists as in winter. Plan building and big expenses so you have enough beds before summer, and keep money aside for the quiet winter months.</string>
    <string name="is_g_stay_t">Beds first</string>
    <string name="is_g_stay">Tourists first pick a place to sleep: they compare appeal, quality, price, location, reputation and advertising of every hotel on the island. Those who find nothing they like don\'t come at all. Then they visit restaurants, bars, shops and attractions around their hotel; the closer a venue is, the more visitors it gets.</string>
    <string name="is_g_loc_t">Location</string>
    <string name="is_g_loc">Being close to the sea is the biggest plus, especially for luxury guests. Forests, the sea, parks, palms and flower beds make an area more beautiful. Noisy places such as discos, pubs, funfairs and the airport put off hotel guests nearby, luxury guests most of all. Hotels with plenty of venues around them are more popular.</string>
    <string name="is_g_price_t">Prices and price wars</string>
    <string name="is_g_price">Tap one of your buildings to change its price. Cheaper prices steal guests from rivals but earn less per guest; every guest also has an operating cost. Rivals cut prices when they lose guests, so watch occupancy and income rather than just the number of guests.</string>
    <string name="is_g_land_t">Land</string>
    <string name="is_g_money_t">Money and the bank</string>
    <string name="is_g_money" formatted="false">Every building has a monthly upkeep, even while empty. The bank lends up to a limit based on your income and assets; instalments are paid at the end of each month. A negative balance costs 1.5% interest per month and counts towards bankruptcy.</string>
    <string name="is_g_rivals_t">Beating your rivals</string>
    <string name="is_g_rivals">Advertising makes your buildings more attractive to one class of tourist for 30 days. Dirty tricks can close a rival\'s building, damage their reputation or trigger a strike, but you may get caught and fined. You can only do one every 30 days. When a rival goes bankrupt, bid for their best buildings in the auctions.</string>
    <string name="is_g_tips_t">Starting tips</string>
    <string name="is_g_tips">Start with affordable beds near the beach, such as a campsite, guesthouse or bungalows, plus a snack kiosk or beach club nearby. Expand when your occupancy is high. Don\'t spend all your money: keep enough for a few months of upkeep. Pause the game whenever you need time to think.</string>
